## 6. Summary mapping PRD → starter template

| PRD capability                  | Files to touch / add                                                        |
| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Letta API key & base URL config | `package.json` (preferences), `useLettaClient.ts`                           |
| Global “show reasoning” toggle  | `package.json` (preferences), `useLettaClient.ts`, `useChat.ts`, `chat.tsx` |
| Agent listing & selection       | `agents.tsx`, `useAgents.ts`, `useLettaClient.ts`                           |
| Core chat with active agent     | `chat.tsx`, `useChat.ts`, `useLettaClient.ts`, `useAgents.ts`               |
| Agent creation from template    | `create-agent.tsx`, `useAgents.ts`                                          |
| Memory block list & inspect     | `memory.tsx`, `useLettaClient.ts`                                           |
| Extension metadata & commands   | `package.json`, `assets/*`                                                  |

This gives you a clean landing zone: clone the starter, make the manifest and dependency changes, drop in these hooks/commands, and you’ll have a Raycast extension that mirrors the core Telegram‑to‑Letta behavior in a desktop‑native way.

